---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { journal, subjects } from '../data/site';
import { u } from '../lib/url';
---

<Base
  title="Aims & Scope"
  description="Learn about the aims, scope, and subject areas of the Algerian Journal of Applied Mathematics (AJAM), a diamond open-access peer-reviewed journal published by the Laboratory of Applied Mathematics at Kasdi Merbah University, Ouargla."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="About the journal"
    title="Aims & Scope"
    subtitle="Original research, surveys, and computational studies across applied and computational mathematics — free to read, free to publish."
  />

  <!-- INTRODUCTION -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="lead">
        The <strong>{journal.title}</strong> (AJAM) is a peer-reviewed, diamond open-access journal
        published by the <strong>{journal.publisher}</strong> at <strong>{journal.institution}</strong>,
        Algeria. The journal publishes original research articles, high-quality survey and review
        papers, and significant computational studies across the breadth of applied and computational
        mathematics. AJAM operates under a diamond open-access model: there are no article-processing
        charges for authors and no subscription fees for readers, ensuring that mathematical
        scholarship is freely and permanently accessible to all.
      </p>
      <p>
        AJAM welcomes contributions from researchers worldwide. While the journal is rooted in the
        Algerian academic tradition, its editorial board, authorship, and readership are explicitly
        international in scope. All submissions undergo rigorous double-blind peer review coordinated
        through an Open Journal Systems (OJS) platform, in accordance with the ethical standards of
        the Committee on Publication Ethics (COPE).
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- AIMS -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Mission</p>
      <h2>Aims of the journal</h2>
      <p>
        AJAM is guided by the following core objectives:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Advance applied and computational mathematics.</strong> Promote high-quality
          original research that extends the frontiers of mathematical theory and its applications
          in science, engineering, and industry.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Bridge theory and application.</strong> Provide a venue that values both rigorous
          mathematical foundations and their practical relevance, encouraging papers that connect
          abstract results with real-world modelling, simulation, or algorithmic development.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Serve the Algerian and international research community.</strong> Offer a
          high-visibility publication channel that strengthens ties between Algerian institutions
          and the global mathematical community, facilitating scientific exchange without geographic
          or economic barriers.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Ensure free and unrestricted dissemination of knowledge.</strong> Through diamond
          open access and the Creative Commons CC BY 4.0 licence, AJAM guarantees that all
          published content can be freely read, shared, and built upon by anyone, in perpetuity.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Support early-career researchers.</strong> Provide a fair, transparent, and
          constructive review process that mentors doctoral students and junior faculty, helping
          them publish their first peer-reviewed results alongside established scholars.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SUBJECT AREAS -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Coverage</p>
      <h2>Scope and subject areas</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        AJAM considers manuscripts in, but not limited to, the following areas of applied and
        computational mathematics:
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid--4 subjects-grid">
        {subjects.map((s) => (
          <div class="card card--accent subject-card">
            <span class="subject-icon" aria-hidden="true">{s.icon}</span>
            <span class="subject-name">{s.name}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
        Interdisciplinary work that applies mathematical methods to problems in physics, biology,
        economics, environmental science, or engineering is equally welcome, provided the
        mathematical contribution is central and substantial.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ARTICLE TYPES -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Submission types</p>
      <h2>Article types we publish</h2>
      <p>
        Authors should indicate the article type at submission. Indicative page lengths refer to
        the final published PDF using the AJAM LaTeX template.
      </p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table class="table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Article type</th>
              <th>Description</th>
              <th>Indicative length</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Original Research Article</strong></td>
              <td>A complete study presenting new theoretical results, proofs, or methodologies, with full derivations and discussion.</td>
              <td>12–30 pages</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Review / Survey Article</strong></td>
              <td>A comprehensive, critical synthesis of a research area; must provide new insights or a structured perspective beyond a literature list.</td>
              <td>20–50 pages</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Short Communication</strong></td>
              <td>A concise report of a focused, self-contained result or observation that merits rapid dissemination.</td>
              <td>4–10 pages</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Computational / Software Note</strong></td>
              <td>Description and validation of a novel algorithm, numerical scheme, or open-source mathematical software package, with reproducible benchmarks.</td>
              <td>6–15 pages</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Letter to the Editor</strong></td>
              <td>A brief, scholarly comment on a recently published AJAM article, including corrections, extensions, or alternative interpretations; author response may be published alongside.</td>
              <td>1–4 pages</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- OUT OF SCOPE -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Editorial policy</p>
      <h2>What AJAM does not consider</h2>
      <p>
        To maintain focus and quality, the following categories of manuscripts fall outside the
        scope of AJAM and will be returned without external review:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Purely pedagogical or expository notes</strong> that do not contain original
          mathematical results or a substantive new perspective for a research audience.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Numerical or computational claims unsupported by methodological detail</strong>
          — results obtained by black-box software without documented algorithms, convergence
          analysis, or reproducibility information will not be considered.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Plagiarised, duplicate, or concurrent submissions.</strong> Manuscripts under
          review elsewhere, or that reproduce previously published content without proper
          attribution, are a violation of AJAM's publication ethics and will result in immediate
          rejection and potential notification of the author's institution.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="muted">
        Manuscripts that are out of scope, or that do not meet minimum formatting requirements,
        may be desk-rejected by the Editor-in-Chief prior to peer review.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CLOSING NOTICE -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="notice">
        <strong>Ready to submit?</strong> AJAM welcomes original contributions from researchers at
        all career stages and from any country. Submissions are handled through our Open Journal
        Systems platform. Please consult the{' '}
        <a href={u('/for-authors/')}>Author Guidelines</a> for full preparation and submission
        instructions, including LaTeX template download, ethical requirements, and review timelines.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .subjects-grid {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .subject-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .subject-icon {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 44px;
    height: 44px;
    background: var(--green-100);
    color: var(--green-700);
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .subject-name {
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
</style>
